A full match checks one value against a sequence of patterns.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    if score is {
        case < 0: io.line("invalid")
        case 0: io.line("zero")
        case >= 90: io.line("excellent")
        else: io.line("other")
    }
]

### Match shape

- The match evaluates its subject once and checks arms in source order.
- Each pattern arm begins a logical line with `case`. An optional `if` guard follows the pattern and must evaluate to Bool.
- A colon ends the header. The arm body starts on that line or continues on later lines.
- The next arm at the same match depth or the closing brace ends the body. Captures belong to that arm's guard and body.
- The first matching arm with a true or omitted guard runs. A selected arm never falls through to its neighbour.

A new `case` starts an arm even if its colon is missing. The diagnostic belongs at that arm header. A line beginning with `is` can instead continue a comparison in the preceding statement. A colon inside a nested template belongs to the template. See @../language-overview/#blocks-and-statements (Blocks and statements).

### Default arm

`else:` is the only catch-all arm.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    if value is {
        case 0: io.line("zero")
        else:
    }
]

In a statement match, bodyless `else:` explicitly ignores every remaining
case.

`case _:` is not wildcard syntax. `else: _` is also invalid.

### Value-producing match

A match can produce values with `then` at a closed receiving site.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    label = if status is {
        case Ready: then "ready"
        case Waiting: then "waiting"
    }
]

Every selected value-producing arm must produce the receiver's required values
or leave the value-producing block, including through `break` or `continue`
targeting an enclosing loop.

A standalone Never call may complete an arm because that arm diverges rather
than producing a value. The arm still does not produce the receiver's type.
At least one selected path must produce values.

### Single-predicate value match

A closed receiver can also use one option-present capture or one choice-variant
predicate. Both forms require a bare `else`. The inline form keeps both results on one line. The block form encloses both branches in one brace pair.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    label = if maybe_name is |name| then name else "guest"

    block_label = if maybe_name is |name| {
        then name
    else
        then "guest"
    }

    score = if status is Ready then 1 else 0

    block_score = if status is Ready {
        then 1
    else
        then 0
    }
]
